From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: YANG JOO WOONG <yjw.cpa@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Apr 2026 10:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: Try BAR resize even when no window was released (v6.18 port)

This is a v6.18 port of Ilpo Järvinen's "PCI: Try BAR resize even when no
window was released" (v2 04/11 series, LKML 2025-11-13, target Linux 6.19).

Symptom on yw1/yw2/yw3 (ASUS X99-E WS, 2× R9700 32GB, slot 1+3 = same PLX A):
  After Phase 1 (rebar-surgery DS) extends PLX A upstream + downstream
  bridge windows to 64GB total via setpci, amdgpu's resource0_resize sysfs
  path still fails because pbus_reassign_bridge_resources() requires at
  least one bridge window to be _released_ before allowing the resize,
  even when the bridge window is already large enough to accommodate the
  new BAR.

Root cause: `pbus_reassign_bridge_resources()` in drivers/pci/setup-bus.c
gates the resize on `if (list_empty(&saved))` — i.e. it only proceeds
when some upstream bridge window was actually released (via
`pci_release_resource()` inside the while loop). With surgery already
having made the windows large, no release happens (every bridge window
is already in use by `res->child`), so `saved` stays empty and the
function returns -ENOENT.

Fix: change the gate to `if (!bridge)` — i.e. proceed whenever a valid
bridge was traversed, even without any window release. Firmware (or our
pre-resize surgery) may have made the window large enough already.
`bridge` is set inside the while loop on each iteration, so it is NULL
only when the loop never ran (root bus case, where there is nothing to
do anyway and the original abort still applies).

NOTE on v6.18 vs v6.19 location:
  - In v6.19 (Ilpo v2 series) the equivalent check moved into
    `pci_resize_resource()` in drivers/pci/setup-res.c after a larger
    refactor that splits release/reassign into helpers.
  - In v6.18 the same `if (list_empty(&saved))` check still lives in
    `pbus_reassign_bridge_resources()` in drivers/pci/setup-bus.c (called
    from pci_resize_resource via dev->bus->self path). We patch v6.18 in
    place rather than backport the entire 11-patch refactor.

Upstream reference:
  v2 04/11: https://lkml.org/lkml/2025/11/13/1292
  Target: Linux 6.19 merge window (Bjorn Helgaas pci-next)

Tested on: Talos Linux v1.12.7 (kernel 6.18.24) — yw3 with 2× R9700.

Signed-off-by: YANG JOO WOONG <yjw.cpa@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/pci/setup-bus.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/setup-bus.c b/drivers/pci/setup-bus.c
--- a/drivers/pci/setup-bus.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/setup-bus.c
@@ -2459,7 +2459,13 @@ int pbus_reassign_bridge_resources(struct pci_bus *bus, struct resource *res)
 		bus = bus->parent;
 	}

-	if (list_empty(&saved)) {
+	if (!bridge) {
+		/*
+		 * Loop never ran (root bus). Nothing to reassign — abort.
+		 * If saved is empty but bridge is set, firmware (or a
+		 * pre-resize surgery) made the windows large enough already;
+		 * proceed with __pci_bus_size_bridges() to try the new size.
+		 */
 		up_read(&pci_bus_sem);
 		return -ENOENT;
 	}
